  "worked_solution": "Let's plot $z$ in the complex plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929099/assets/78399e67e0ba69c1d7848a41aa5d4a5f8040fc578aab30a99f7e19ac86ece179.png)\n\nThe complex number $z$ lies in the fourth quadrant of the complex plane. Hence $\\frac{3\\pi }{2}<arg\u2061(z)<2\\pi .$ \n\nIf $\\alpha $ is the angle that $z$ makes with the positive real axis, then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}tan\u2061\\alpha  & =\\frac{8}{8\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ \\alpha  & =arctan\\,(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =arg\u2061(z)=2\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{6}=\\frac{11\\pi }{6}.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
